# Gate step 1004-vsh2 — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# SECOND near-drop in twenty minutes, and the reason the freeze exists. This
# region gains a step every time any host lands a fixture, so a 32-minute gate
# on this box cannot win the race by construction: gate 22 raced yolanda's jq
# fixture, gate 23 raced this one. Resolving "take my side whole" would have
# removed its only binding both times — a valid file with an entry dropped,
# which bash -n cannot see. Prefix 045 sits between 040 and 050; the ten-spacing
# is there so a step can land between two without renaming either.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose: a binding assembled from a
# variable is invisible to every name-based scan, including the
# bound-or-retired guard (1063-nraf). Keep it a plain string.
#
# Yolanda's rationale, carried over verbatim: the predicate matched on every run
# including a clean one, and the same predicate gated the delete, so the guard
# never guarded. A predicate that cannot be false is not a check. On a Windows
# host the fixture RUNS the shipped predicate against a target that does not
# exist and requires false, with the original spelling as the control;
# elsewhere that arm skips rather than asserting from prose.
STEP_DESC="Checking the smoke runbook's credential predicate can be false (1004-vsh2)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-cmdkey-predicate-discriminates.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the smoke runbook's credential-presence predicate cannot be false, or the helper is gone (1004-vsh2) — see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Credential predicate check passed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="yolanda 2026-11-25 msys ok:cmdkey-predicate:4 arms; macbookair 2026-11-25 darwin 2 arms (3 and 4 are Windows only)"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/test-cmdkey-predicate-discriminates.lua skills/smoke-curl-install-and-test-e2e/SKILL.md"
# ORDER 2184-sinp: DECLARED INPUTS (2118-tnut grammar). The one repo file
# the script reads is the smoke runbook whose predicate it extracts. An ATIME
# TRACE of a real run (twice) read only that and the script.
STEP_INPUTS="path:skills/smoke-curl-install-and-test-e2e/SKILL.md"
